analysis.&lt;br/&gt; *&lt;br/&gt; * This analyzer parses AMBA AXI protocol signals and converts them into high-level transaction records. AXI is ARM&amp;apos;s high-performance interconnect&lt;br/&gt; * protocol widely used in SoC designs for connecting processors, memory controllers, and peripherals with support for out-of-order transaction&lt;br/&gt; * completion and burst transfers.&lt;br/&gt; *&lt;br/&gt; * Key features implemented by this analyzer: - Support for both AXI3 and AXI4 protocol versions with automatic detection - Five-channel&lt;br/&gt; * architecture tracking: write address (AW), write data (W), write response (B), read address (AR), and read data (R) - Transaction correlation&lt;br/&gt; * using ID-based matching across channels - Burst transaction handling with configurable burst types (FIXED, INCR, WRAP) - Automatic data size&lt;br/&gt; * calculation from AWSIZE/ARSIZE and AWLEN/ARLEN - Out-of-order transaction completion support - AXI3 write data interleaving detection via WID&lt;br/&gt; * signal - AXI4 QoS and region support - Protection, cache, and lock attribute tracking&lt;br/&gt; *&lt;br/&gt; * The analyzer processes five independent AXI channels with handshake-based transfers: - Write Address (AW): Master initiates write with address&lt;br/&gt; * and control (AWVALID/AWREADY) - Write Data (W): Master provides write data beats with byte strobes (WVALID/WREADY) - Write Response (B): Slave&lt;br/&gt; * acknowledges write completion with status (BVALID/BREADY) - Read Address (AR): Master initiates read with address and control (ARVALID/ARREADY)&lt;br/&gt; * - Read Data (R): Slave returns read data beats with status (RVALID/RREADY)&lt;br/&gt; *&lt;br/&gt; * Transaction matching uses ID-based correlation: - Write transactions: AWID creates transaction, WID matches data (AXI3 only), BID matches&lt;br/&gt; * response - Read transactions: ARID creates transaction, RID matches response data beats - Multiple outstanding transactions per ID are supported&lt;br/&gt; * - AXI3 interleaving: WID allows data from different transactions to be interleaved&lt;br/&gt; *&lt;br/&gt; * Protocol version detection: - AXI3: Identified by presence of WID signal (write data interleaving) - AXI4: Identified by QoS/Region signals and&lt;br/&gt; * absence of WID - Automatic fallback when version cannot be determined&lt;br/&gt; *&lt;br/&gt; * Implementation Notes: - Operates on rising clock edges with optional active-low reset handling - Automatically calculates transfer sizes from&lt;br/&gt; * burst length and size parameters - Burst length encoding: AWLEN/ARLEN = (number of beats - 1) - Burst size encoding: bytes per beat = 2^(AWSIZE/ARSIZE)&lt;br/&gt; * - Supports byte lane strobes (WSTRB) for partial writes - Response tracking with OKAY, EXOKAY, SLVERR, and DECERR codes&lt;br/&gt; *&lt;br/&gt; * Copyright (c) 2013-2025 Thomas Haber All rights reserved.&lt;br/&gt; */&lt;br/&gt;@RegistryAnnotation(annotation = AxiAnalyzer.Annotation.class)&lt;br/&gt;public class AxiAnalyzer extends AbstractPinlevelAnalyzer {&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;    public static class Annotation {&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;        public static final String id = &amp;quot;de.toem.impulse.processor.axiAnaylzer&amp;quot;;&lt;br/&gt;        public static final String label = I18n.Processor_AxiAnalyzer;&lt;br/&gt;        public static final String description = I18n.Processor_AxiAnalyzer_Description;&lt;br/&gt;        public static final String iconId = I18n.Processor_AxiAnalyzer_IconId;&lt;br/&gt;        public static final String helpURL = I18n.Processor_AxiAnalyzer_HelpURL;&lt;br/&gt;        public static final String certificate = &amp;quot;JE4iLUNxkgRH5MXevPFzRslhKPfxhOTb\nVhODxCEfY7ExnE2ylazpEwuuq2EVmdJT\nucEnDOe7QJEU6uVBl8aJVTRGMZxjJjns\nBBW7aD2RbKwHviueknU5D/EICU78GLSX\nNTgeXLjBPXS8gPZLO94dJ2Sw7mH2xpvu\ngvx8HlqqzpeYDxz+5fm1jS7cOQ+pEH1v\nzfRVBB5ZwoTho2+5weq52z2q/4C5axaO\nmgZEiPcF9WKNAB1PCG9tzSE73px5vJht\nLenZ381b8Zkwd3Fzn9B8Hdb32qaNQtj0\nyoST6DQac3BxzPvpUvAapRK2eb6